            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "I have a use-case for this:\n\nbuffer:\n```\nif (v.type == \"a\") {\n  ...\n} else if (v.type == \"b\"\n  || v.type == \"c\") {\n  ..\n}\n```\n\n`/v\\.type<CR>1Q` cursors on, primary cursor is on the first match\n`^vfe`\n\nvisual is like so:\n```\nif (v.type == \"a\") {\n^~~~~~~~~~\n  ...\n} else if (v.type == \"b\"\n^~~~~~\n  || v.type == \"c\") {\n^~~~~~~~~~~\n  ..\n}\n```\n\n`;` jump to next 'e' where possible. The intention is to visual-select like so:\n```\nif (v.type == \"a\") {\n^~~~~~~~~~\n  ...\n} else if (v.type == \"b\"\n^~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^^            <--- newly extended visual selection\n  || v.type == \"c\") {\n^~~~~~~~~~~\n  ..\n}\n```\n\nBut because the primary cursor has no 'e' to find, the motion isn't cascaded",
